=== Honesty-covenant notes (rule 9: no silent drift) ===
1. Path: the prompt's allowed path 'com/teslasync/dashboard-widgets/GeofenceWidget.*' is honored verbatim for the
   directory; the Kotlin package is 'io.teslasync.android.dashboard.widgets.geofence' (a hyphenated/PascalCase
   directory cannot be a valid package). This matches every existing P3 dashboard-widget sibling
   (e.g. DestinationETAWidget). InvalidPackageDeclaration/MatchingDeclarationName are suppressed per file.
2. Gate task path: the prompt gate's ':app:' qualifier does not exist; settings.gradle.kts maps the module to
   ':android' (its own comment: 'every P3/A* prompt gate addresses :android:'). Ran the unqualified/':android:'
   equivalents (assembleRelease / testReleaseUnitTest / ktlintCheck detekt), which resolve to ':android:'.
3. i18n: all 7 web keys (widget.geofence.title/noZone/noFences/radius/disabled/inside/outside) already exist in the
   P1/S10 catalog as translation_widget_geofence_* (en/ar/he) — no strings.xml change needed or made.
4. Error state (parity): the web GeofenceWidget does NOT pass WidgetShell's 'error' prop, so it never renders a full
   QueryError body. It surfaces fetch failures via the WidgetShell DataFreshness chip (error/offline) + the refresh
   affordance, keeping the best-effort fence list / empty body visible. Reproduced verbatim: the combine yields a
   cache-carrying Resource.Error -> UiState Content/Empty + stale + errorKind (offline chip + refresh = retry); no
   separate hard-error surface. Loading is the only WidgetShell short-circuit (-> skeleton), matching the source.
5. Compact freshness (minor, documented): the web compact branch wires only the vehicle-state query's freshness to
   its (title-less) WidgetShell; the native surface uses the merged (state+geofences) freshness in both footprints.
   This is strictly more correct (the zone depends on both feeds) and avoids a second UiState; behavior is identical
   in every non-error case.
6. Map render in UI test: the map footprint (rows>=3 with coords) needs Play Services, so the instrumented render
   tests pin deterministic map-free footprints (rows<3 / no coords). The map composition (TeslaMap + Circle +
   MapDotMarker) is compiled by assembleRelease and the maps layer is covered by existing shared maps tests.
7. Pre-existing, out-of-scope: ':android:compileDebugAndroidTestKotlin' fails on TWO unrelated sibling files
   (BatteryCellsWidgetUiTest.kt, DriveEfficiencyChartWidgetUiTest.kt: unresolved assertExists/assertDoesNotExist).
   This is NOT caused by this change, is NOT a gate step (the gate compiles+runs only unit tests, never androidTest),
   and those files are outside this artifact's allowed files, so they were not modified. GeofenceWidgetUiTest.kt uses
   only the same imports as the compiling DestinationETAWidgetUiTest sibling.

